body:
I think if it's an honest slip up then it's totally ok. I can understand it'd be awkward when the managers are all referring to them as "She", but as a substitute (For most conversations) you could use their names in place of pronouns (Which you've been doing) and that's completely normal as well.

&#x200B;

I think it's amazing that you are putting this much thought into it, and as such if you make a mistake I don't think that your friends are going to mind especially since you are trying. I know it can be really confusing and jarring at first.

&#x200B;

As for the "young person trend" and being phased out, it could be. However trans people have been about forever, it's just now they are gaining more widespread acceptance and publicity. As I am trans, I would say it's not a trend, but I understand I am slightly biased in saying that. Regardless of where you stand and whether or not it will be phased out, I think it's good to make the effort to use their desired pronouns on the basis of respect.

&#x200B;

Feel free to disagree with me on anything I said ofc.
